# The native build target.
#
# Loaded by `vite build --mode native` (see `npm run build:native`) and by
# nothing else, so the website's build is untouched by it. Vite exposes every
# `VITE_`-prefixed variable from the mode's env file as `import.meta.env`, and
# the game reads this one in `src/platform/target.ts` to decide whether it is a
# browser build or a packaged one:
#
#   web     — the website and the PWA. Service worker, install offer, update bar.
#   mobile  — the Android/iOS shell. None of those, because a packaged
#             application is already installed and its assets already local.
#   desktop — the future Steam build, for the same reasons as `mobile`.
#
# The value is validated where it is read: anything unrecognised falls back to
# `web`, so a build that says nothing is the build that already works.
VITE_BUILD_TARGET=mobile
